$ Warped CQUAD4 (default QUAD4TYP MIN4, QUADAXIS SPLITD) given a small rigid rotation w = (1e-3, 2e-3, 0)
$ about the origin: grids 1-3 are held at the rigid motion (translations w x r, rotations w); grid 4 is free.
$ A rigid element leaves grid 4 on the same rigid motion:
$   T1 = 6.0E-4, T2 = -3.0E-4, T3 = 5.0E-3, R1 = 1.0E-3, R2 = 2.0E-3.
$ The quad is warped (HBAR = 0.3) and not symmetric about side 1-2 (QUAD_DELTA /= 0), which tests the
$ warp transform BMEAN in the element axes the membrane stiffness uses.
SOL 101
CEND
TITLE = WARPED QUAD4 RIGID ROTATION, MIN4
SPC = 1
DISP = ALL
SPCFORCE = ALL
BEGIN BULK
GRID,1,,0.0,0.0,-0.3
GRID,2,,10.0,0.0,0.3
GRID,3,,12.0,8.0,-0.3
GRID,4,,1.0,7.0,0.3
CQUAD4,1,1,1,2,3,4
PSHELL,1,1,0.1,1,,1
MAT1,1,1.E7,,0.3
SPC,1,1,1,-6.0-4
SPC,1,1,2,3.0-4
SPC,1,1,3,0.
SPC,1,1,4,1.0-3
SPC,1,1,5,2.0-3
SPC,1,1,6,0.
SPC,1,2,1,6.0-4
SPC,1,2,2,-3.0-4
SPC,1,2,3,-2.0-2
SPC,1,2,4,1.0-3
SPC,1,2,5,2.0-3
SPC,1,2,6,0.
SPC,1,3,1,-6.0-4
SPC,1,3,2,3.0-4
SPC,1,3,3,-1.6-2
SPC,1,3,4,1.0-3
SPC,1,3,5,2.0-3
SPC,1,3,6,0.
ENDDATA
